TASK-4 COMPUTATION

Each request carries immutable:

4-bit input x0;
stage-A truth-table program PA;
stage-B truth-table program PB;
stage-C truth-table program PC;
stage-D truth-table program PD;
stream;
creation epoch;
deterministic request id.

Interpreter remains the exact 4-bit truth-table interpreter.

Stage A:

yA = PA(x0)

x1 replaces bit 0 of x0 with yA.

Stage B:

yB = PB(x1)

x2 replaces bit 1 of x1 with yB.

Stage C:

yC = PC(x2)

x3 replaces bit 2 of x2 with yC.

Stage D:

yD = PD(x3)

Verified answer:
yD.

Every request therefore requires four causally ordered PROCESS operations.

LIFECYCLE

RAW
-> SENSED
-> PROCESSED_A
-> PROCESSED_B
-> PROCESSED_C
-> PROCESSED_D
-> ROUTING
-> AT_EGRESS
-> VERIFIED
-> DONE.

No stage may be skipped.

Verification recomputes A, B, C, and D from immutable provenance.

Verification failure enters REPAIR_PENDING.

REPAIR recomputes all four stages from immutable x0 / PA / PB / PC / PD.

Independent re-verification remains mandatory before DONE.

